From e14a0b4419dc3e6818d3b03a64caa5eb3b91f643 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeni Tennison <jeni@jenitennison.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:16:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Deploy docs: the UpCloud firewall, outgoing mail, what to do
 when email does not send

From the first real deploy: a trial UpCloud account cannot edit its firewall (and it resets
once the limits are lifted), so outgoing connections to Scaleway on 465 timed out. Documents the
rules the server needs, why outgoing stays open, how to read the app's SMTP log, and the first
deliverability result. The wizard now tests that the server can reach Scaleway's mail server
before asking for the SMTP details, labels the username as the Project ID and the password as
the API secret key, and checks the app's own SMTP verification after the first deploy.

Part of #17 and #349.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 deploy/setup-wizard.sh | 23 ++++++++++++++--
 docs/deploy.md         | 60 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 81 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

